{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh beveling in blender mesh beveling in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","fileName":"Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh Beveling in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh beveling in blender mesh beveling in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","fileName":"Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh Beveling in Blender","heading":"Mesh Beveling in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Beveling replaces a sharp mesh corner with additional geometry that forms a rounded or flattened transition. Even objects perceived as sharp usually have a small edge radius, so bevels help a model respond to light more plausibly.\n\nThe Bevel tool works on selected components and can vary the width and segmentation of the transition. It adds detail where a perfectly mathematical corner would look unnaturally harsh.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Beveling in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"